# Context: EdTech Live Virtual Classroom SaaS (Next.js App Router)

## Core System Architecture & Rules
- ALWAYS read and analyze existing codebase context before generating modifications.
- NEVER delete, overwrite, or break working functionality unless explicitly instructed.
- Strictly enforce Role-Based Access Control (RBAC): MANAGER, TEACHER, STUDENT.
- Strict Privacy Rule: NEVER expose user email addresses or phone numbers between Teachers and Students. All interaction must be masked using internal User_IDs.

## Tech Stack Requirements
- Framework: Next.js (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS
- Database & ORM: Prisma ORM (PostgreSQL/Supabase)
- Video Engine: Daily.co (@daily-co/daily-react)
  - Video streams inside the app portal.
  - Automatic background recording enabled on server.
  - NO recording buttons or controls allowed for teachers or students.
- Collaborative Canvas: Excalidraw (@excalidraw/excalidraw)
  - Loaded dynamically client-side (`ssr: false`).
  - Image drag-and-drop enabled.
  - Expose `exportBoardToPdf()` utility to render board state into a PDF Blob upon lesson completion.
- In-App Chat: Stream Chat (`stream-chat-react`)
  - Auto-moderation filters enabled to censor phone numbers and emails.
  - Allow PDF, DOC, and image file attachments.
  - Access restricted exclusively to lesson's Student, Teacher, and Manager.
- WhatsApp & Notifications:
  - Send lesson end summary via WhatsApp API.
  - Attach board PDF directly as a document.
  - Include secure streaming link for video recording (do NOT send video raw files).